{
 "slug": "toggl-mobile-timer",
 "module": "toggl-mobile-timer/src/logic",
 "function": "evalVector",
 "note": "args = [fn, args]: fn names an exported function of src/logic.ts and args is its argument list, so each case is {name, fn, args, expected}. Times are fixed instants; day cases use UTC, UTC+7 (420) and UTC-5 (-300). Expected values are written by hand; millisecond values come from Python datetime, not from the TypeScript code. Toggl rules checked here: 30 requests an hour on the free plan, HTTP 402 when the quota is used up, HTTP 429 from the leaky bucket, back off and do not repeat (engineering.toggl.com/docs/track/, support.toggl.com/api-webhook-limits; raw copies in research/obsidian-run/raw/u8b).",
